description.narrative:
The objective of the Initiative is to contribute to the sustainable green transition and increase income, create jobs for ethnic minority women in A Luoi 2 and A Luoi 4 communes, Hue city in the central region of Viet Nam, through promoting the development of themedicinal plant value chain under the forest canopy, responding to the impacts of climate change.
Main activities include:
(i) For the Outcome 1: Initial assessment combined with survey and assessment of the current status of the growing area and the current medicinal herb processing process of the cooperatives; Organize training on techniques for planting, harvesting, and processing medicinal herbs according to sustainable standards (OCOP, VietGAP) for cooperative/production group members; and Support women-owned cooperatives (or those with a majority of female members) to establish on-site medicinal herb processing and preservation systems;
(ii) Forthe Outcome 2: Support the establishment of a joint medicinal plant production facility managed by women; Organize training on production and business planning for women in the Cooperative Management Board and heads of production groups; Organize training on leadership, negotiation and decision-making skills for women participating in managementboards of cooperatives and production groups; and Organize regular mentoring sessions for women leaders of cooperatives/production groups to share, support and connect;
(iii) For the Outcome 3: Survey market demand and identify potential MSMEs to link with female-owned medicinal cooperatives (or with a majorityof female members); Support female-owned cooperatives (or those with a majority of female members) to develop and upgrade products from medicinal herbs; Support in building brand identity, labels,green packaging and professional product profiles for key medicinalproducts; Connecting female-owned (or majority female-member) cooperatives to participate in green markets or trade promotion events; Promoting regional linkages with cooperatives/production groups producing medicinal materials; and final evaluation.
